  "issue": {
    "headline": "CPS Energy and SAWS answer to the city, and to no voter directly",
    "body": "San Antonio owns its electric and gas utility and its water system. Their boards are appointed, not elected, and their rate cases, fuel-cost recoveries and capital plans move more money than most line items in the City budget. They are public bodies, so their board packets are public records.",
    "record": "CPS Energy and San Antonio Water System board packets, rate-case filings and the annual transfer to the City's general fund."
